@startuml 03_Auth_No_Device_Available

title 03. User Authenticate - No Other Device Available

actor User
participant "Client App" as Client
participant "Device Storage" as Storage
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Email Service" as Email

User -> Client: Login (email, password)
activate Client

Client -> Server: POST /auth/login\n{email, password}
activate Server
Server --> Client: 200 OK\n{session_token}
deactivate Server

Client -> Storage: Check for identity_secret
activate Storage
Storage --> Client: NOT FOUND
deactivate Storage

Client --> User: "No identity secret found"
deactivate Client

User -> Client: "No other device available"
activate Client

Client -> Server: POST /auth/identity-reset/request
activate Server

Server -> Server: Generate verification token\n(short-lived, single-use)

Server -> Email: Send verification email\n{verification_link}
activate Email
Email --> User: Email with verification link
deactivate Email

Server --> Client: "Verification email sent"
deactivate Server

Client --> User: "Check your email"
deactivate Client

User -> User: Open email\nClick verification link

User -> Server: GET /auth/identity-reset/verify\n?token={verification_token}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Verify token:\n- Valid?\n- Not expired?\n- Not already used?

alt Token valid
    Server -> DB: Get user's conversations
    activate DB
    DB --> Server: List of conversation IDs
    deactivate DB
    
    loop For each conversation
        Server -> DB: UPDATE conversations\nSET member_key = NULL\nWHERE user_id = {user_id}
        activate DB
        DB --> Server: Updated
        deactivate DB
    end
    
    Server -> DB: Mark token as used
    activate DB
    DB --> Server: Done
    deactivate DB
    
    Server --> Client: 200 OK\n"Reset successful"
    
else Token invalid
    Server --> Client: 401 Unauthorized\n"Invalid or expired token"
end

deactivate Server

activate Client
Client -> Client: Generate NEW identity_secret
note right of Client
  Fresh identity secret generated
  User will need to get group keys
  from other members for all
  conversations
end note

Client -> Storage: Store new identity_secret
activate Storage
Storage --> Client: Stored
deactivate Storage

Client --> User: "New identity created\nYou'll need group keys from members"
deactivate Client

note over User, DB
  Result:
  ✅ User has new identity_secret
  ✅ All member_keys set to NULL
  ⚠️ User locked out of conversations
  ⚠️ Needs group keys from online members
end note

@enduml
